{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The current model passes target-match detail and temporal detail separately to its adapters; it has no explicit summary of how target-match detail varies across history blocks. I’ll prepare four equally sized variants: an ordered interaction, a scrambled-order control, and two duplicate-summary controls. The existing click improvement also comes with lower auxiliary-task AUCs, so the proposal will retain that tradeoff and keep all new performance claims pending host evaluation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('/workspace/runtime_context.json'))\nfixed=['protocol '+r['required_study_protocol_ref'],'all released fields/labels/prefix and masks; official_offline visibility','one epoch, seed20262027, batch8192, bf16, split optimizers and sum four BCE','embedding/tower/scorer architecture, uf routing, gradient ownership, four incumbent summaries','same module allocation/order, five summary contractions, support gate and coefficient builders in all new variants','task-specific adapter routing, residual_hidden16, zero-initialized adapter output']\nvariants=[('joint_ordered','candidate','candidate.py','ordered'),('joint_scrambled','control','control_joint_scrambled.py','scrambled'),('duplicate_match','control','control_duplicate_match.py','duplicate_match'),('duplicate_curvature','control','control_duplicate_curvature.py','duplicate_curvature')]\nconfig=dict(__import__('ast').literal_eval(next(n.value for n in __import__('ast').parse(Path('/workspace/candidate.py').read_text()).body if isinstance(n,__import__('ast').Assign) and any(isinstance(t,__import__('ast').Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))))\nstudy={\n'id':'g0-next-target-match-coarse-order-interaction',\n'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','g2-r0004-context_only','g3-r0003-embedding_item_primary','g0-r0006-compressed_task','g0-r0006-events_task','g0-r0007-anchored_task_query','g0-r0007-anchor_shared_query','g0-r0008-task_contrast','g0-r0008-task_capacity','g0-r0009-match_detail_task','g0-r0010-field_detail_task','g0-r0010-mean_detail_task','g0-r0011-interaction_detail_task','g0-r0011-duplicate_detail_task','g0-r0013-block_task','g0-r0013-duplicate_task','g0-r0014-curvature_task','g0-r0014-duplicate_linear_task','g0-r0014-scrambled_curvature_task','g0-r0015-shared_curvature','g0-r0015-shared_duplicate_linear','g0-r0015-shared_scrambled_curvature'],\n'question':'Does an explicit target-match by coarse-history-order value moment add useful click ranking information beyond the incumbent separate match/local-order/coarse-linear/quadratic summaries, at matched added capacity and operator count?',\n'hypothesis':'Observed limitation: the inspected incumbent concatenates four separately pooled moments before a nonlinear task adapter; it does not expose the value moment of within-block centered target affinity multiplied by block rank. Nonlinear readout of marginal moments cannot in general reconstruct this joint moment. Earlier ordered block and curvature improvements motivate testing this representational uncertainty; they do not establish that this missing direction is predictive. Residualizing the product against match and local ordinal coefficients may retain target-relevant chronological variation discarded by the compression. Ordered residual should outperform scrambled-order and duplicate channels with the same architecture. This is an explicit interaction test, not a claim that target-aware temporal modeling is new.',\n'nearest_work':[\n{'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived DIN primary text establishes target-conditioned local activation and pooling. Retain the adapted action-aware scorer; add a fixed masked cross-moment before task-specific residual readout. No original DIN reproduction or priority claim.'},\n{'source_ref':'unirank-code:UniMixer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned forward lines175-200 flatten the sequence with context for unified tokenization. Our fifth channel is an explicit low-dimensional target-match/order contraction and retains the thirty compressed slots; no flattened learned tokenizer or paired-stream mixing is imported. Original paper not audited; novelty unverified.'},\n{'source_ref':'unirank-code:EST','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned forward lines119-156 preserve sequence tokens and iterate a masked unified interaction stack. Our operator is a single fixed masked residual moment feeding existing task adapters. Original paper not audited; no equivalence or priority claim.'}],\n'inherited_components':['Exact initial candidate.py SHA2568116e9e94f578ba104f1718dc305b3bba647326e918b4759b4e7a48612619b97 from g0-r0014-curvature_task','FeatureEmbeddingDict and shared target/history tables; action-aware DIN scorer and Dice towers','Ten contiguous blocks; uniform click and feedback-stratified auxiliary compressed routes','Auxiliary scorer/item/action gradient blocking; auxiliary context gradients retained','Existing match counts and all four value summaries, task-specific residual bank and zero final layers','All frozen host data/scoring/training interfaces'],\n'proposed_difference':'Append one value-width channel to each adapter input (+4*16*112=7168 dense parameters at frozen schema). Let a be per-event mean of valid item/category/brand exact-match flags, centered within each ten-event block. Let p be within-block centered ordinal and r the coarse block rank. Build a*r and a*fixed-scrambled-r. Project both products twice off the span of p and a (Gram-Schmidt basis), with within-block recentering, in FP32. The resulting directions are also orthogonal to block-constant linear/quadratic channels because they have zero sum within each block. A common gate requires both interaction directions, match norm, local norm and the inherited fourth coefficient to be nondegenerate. Scale each interaction, duplicate a and duplicate quadratic to the same local-ordinal coefficient L2 norm, with the same common gate. Contract five channels against the same masked values and sqrt(valid_count) denominator in every variant. Only the selected fifth coefficient differs. The common gate itself is target/order dependent and is shared by controls; duplicate controls test added direction beyond that shared gate, not strictly absence of any